+# Owner-adopted attempt recovery implementation plan
+
+> Execute with `superpowers:subagent-driven-development`, using the supplied
+> `docs/design/owner-adopted-attempt-recovery.md` as the contract. Do not create
+> worktrees. Commit each implementation handoff step with explicit paths.
+
+**Goal:** Retire an owner-adopted uncommitted attempt whose predecessor lineage
+contains uncovered changes, preserving all v1 behavior.
+
+**Architecture:** Reuse v1 capture/archive/restore mechanics, add a Git-derived
+incident and v2 disposition, and reopen historical evidence through a scoped byte
+overlay. No runtime changes or dependencies.
+
+**Tradeoffs:** New validators must use hooked file readers; diagnostic order is
+contractual; separate strict trailer parsing preserves the old parser.
+
+## Baseline and scope
+
+- Base: `069f713b8b2f1c7f6bb5e5cf31fc1f91c8f5f2cf`.
+- Base log: `/tmp/retirement-recovery-logs/base.log`.
+- Base failed-node list: `/tmp/retirement-recovery-logs/base.failed`.
+- Base command: `python -m pytest -q -n 16 --dist=worksteal -m "not e2e" -rf`
+  in tmux. Result: 71 failed, 6551 passed, 6 skipped, 3 errors, 229.38 seconds.
+- The only pre-existing untracked file was the injected design document. It was
+  preserved; all tracked files were clean before the baseline run.
+- Callers: source bindings; broad-evidence record and review validators;
+  materialization lineage validators; migration capture/validate/apply/postvalidate
+  and CLI; lazy package exports. Existing default calls keep their behavior.
+- Tests: four new modules and a real fixture helper. Existing v1 tests and fixture
+  manifest stay unchanged; only the public export-set assertion gains names.
+- Primary risk: incorrect archived-byte resolution could validate live bytes or
+  corrupt relocation. Reuse exact v1 mutation helpers and verify real relocation.
+
+## Ordered handoff
+
+- [x] 0. Record base and broad failures before edits.
+- [x] 1. Add strict predecessor lineage and real-Git tests; collect, test, commit.
+- [x] 2. Add byte-overlay leaf and scope/fallback tests; collect, test, commit.
+- [x] 3. Hook existing validators, add real-lineage overlay tests; run broad-evidence
+  regression module in tmux, commit.
+- [x] 4. Extract v1 shared helpers without changing check order; run untouched v1
+  tests, commit.
+- [x] 5. Build real generations 1–11 with bootstrap reservation/handoff, broad
+  baseline, pending materialization, owner adoption, Git delta, and authority.
+- [x] 6. Add incident build/preflight/reopening with tests; collect, test, commit.
+- [x] 7. Add v2 structure/live validation, capture/replay, schema dispatch and CLI;
+  real apply/postvalidate and rejection tests; collect, test, commit.
+- [x] 8. Add two lazy exports and update only their expected export-set assertion.
+- [x] 9. Run every supplied verification command in order, CLI smoke, full suite
+  and base comparison. Obtain ordered specification then quality review, fix
+  findings, record evidence and any deviations.
+
+The supplied design's Implementation Handoff and Verification Strategy contain
+the exact per-step contracts, selectors, rejection cases and public smoke.
+
+
+## Final implementation and reviews
+
+The Git predecessor projection, scoped byte overlay, incident builder/validator,
+v2 capture and schema dispatch, reviewed apply/postvalidation, CLI mode and two
+lazy exports are implemented. The temporary-repository fixture uses real ledger
+generations 1–11, including the Task 1 reservation and bootstrap handoff. The four
+new test modules contain 140 tests. V1 tests and the broad fixture manifest are
+unchanged; the only existing test edit adds the two lazy export names.
+
+Ordered independent specification review approved `069f713..826b0b3`, followed by
+independent code-quality approval. Review found an incident binding could use an
+extra disposition row instead of an incident row; commit `35d1c7b` fixes this and
+adds its regression check. Public attestation-pair rejection tests exercise the
+public validation path, beyond the private helper checks.
+
+## Fresh verification evidence
